 "surprises": [
  "The 100,000 lump sum is treated differently. A1, A2 and B1 count the Saver row as spending (MORTGAGE). B2 pairs it with the loan row as a transfer (TRANSFER, X0131), not spending.",
  "B1 has only the Saver leg of the lump sum as a transaction; A1, A2 and B2 also have the ADDITIONAL REPAYMENT row on the home loan account.",
  "A2 keeps 9 card rows dated 16 to 29 Jun 2023 that A1, B1 and B2 do not have (they start 3 Jul 2023). That explains A2's 680 card rows against A1's 671.",
  "Exact repeats outside the windows are deliberate, not re-imports: the 28 Apr 2026 estate credit of 100,000 is split into two 50,000 rows in A1, B1 and B2 (A2 words its second half differently), and B1's two Fairy St Chemist repeats are re-posts as Mum's care after correction rows."
 ]
